vcq|n|A long, narrow boat with a high prow and stern, used in the canals of Venice. A gondola is usually propelled by one or two oarsmen who stand facing the prow, or by poling. A gondola for passengers has a small open cabin amidships, for their protection against the sun or rain. A sumptuary law of Venice required that gondolas should be painted black, and they are customarily so painted now. ; A flat-bottomed boat for freight. ; A long platform car, either having no sides or with very low sides, used on railroads.	a:x50,94,5~x50,94,5
